{'parameter_id': 12, 'term_id': 'TERM-091', 'status': 'active', 'notes': "Promoted from the base vocabulary on the owner's direction of 2026-10-09 (populate the parameter table from the existing terms registry). Judged a measurable design quantity by the session; no source adjudication behind it. Direction left unset until an admitted source states which way is better for a disabled person. || ANNOTATED 2026-10-30 by session_2026-10-30-rest-landing-parameter: Two sentences above no longer hold. 'Direction left unset until an admitted source states which way is better' is superseded: accessibility_direction and direction_rationale now carry it. 'no source adjudication behind it' was false when written (derive: select outcome from term_adjudications where term_id = 'TERM-091'; GAP-067). The owner's 2026-10-30 hypothesis that the problem on a ramp is the lack of a rest landing, and the approval to make landing spacing a headline parameter, are recorded as owner decision D18 and row E7 in workplan/2026-10-30-ramp-spec-pages/RENDER-DECISIONS-AND-PIPELINE.md and in HANDOFF.md section 3; E7 asks that the approval be confirmed, and it is not yet in references/project-standards.md. The maximum run between rests is this parameter's run, so no second parameter was minted (rule 5). The vertical expression is a separate open question (the rise gap).", 'direction_rationale': "A shorter permitted run between landings is more accessible for a disabled person: the admitted sources state the need a landing serves, and none states a longer unbroken run as better. REF-00992 (Approved Document M, para 1.22): 'Some people need to be able to stop frequently; for instance to regain strength or breath, or to ease pain.' REF-00995 (Flemish decree of 5 June 2009, explanatory memorandum to Article 19): a landing is required per 50 cm of level difference or 10 m of ramp 'om de nodige rustpunten te voorzien door te vermijden dat een helling te lang aanhoudt' (to provide the necessary rest points by preventing a ramp continuing too long). REF-00996 states the same mechanism ('zodat voldoende rustpunten ingebouwd worden') but names Article 19 of that decree as its regulation, so it restates REF-00995 and is not a third independent source. Derived from those statements, not adjudicated; no source states the direction as a rule about the run limit itself. NOT contested: no admitted source identifies a population for whom a longer unbroken run is better. The codes pair a shorter run with a steeper permitted gradient (REF-00992 Table 1); that trade belongs to the gradient parameter (3, lower_is_better), not to this one.", 'accessibility_direction': 'lower_is_better'}
